# Shiver Phase 3 Design Document

*Phase 3 (TESD 1100) | Shiver by Kelpkin | Pages, layout, look and feel, and decisions, updated to match the finished build*

## 1. Overview

Phase 3 turns Shiver into a client-side website: the owner dashboard a shop owner would see when they open the app. It has three pages, Overview, Reps, and Posts, built with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. It runs entirely in the browser with sample data, so changes last until the page is reloaded.

This document records the page designs, the look and feel, the phone layout, and the decisions behind them. Where the build differs from the original plan, the difference is listed at the end of Section 2. How the files fit together is covered in `architecture.md`, and the data is covered in `data-model.md`.

Phase 3 builds the owner side only. Shop owners are the main audience, because they install the app and run the PR program. Reps get their own view, the PR Portal, in a later phase once login is added. The design follows the look of Shopify's admin (Polaris), since Shiver will run inside Shopify in Phase 5.

## 2. What Changes from Phase 2

| Area | Phase 2 | Phase 3 |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Platform | JavaFX desktop app | Website that runs in any browser |
| Languages | Java | HTML, CSS, and JavaScript |
| Screens | One window with four tabs | Three pages linked by a sidebar |
| Team list | Team tab | Reps page with filter tabs, search, and sort |
| Logging posts | Log Post tab, every post counts right away | Posts page with a review step: pending posts are approved or rejected |
| History | View History window | Rep side panel with codes, social accounts, stats, and history |
| Summary view | None | Overview page with metric cards, a chart, a review list, and top reps |
| Rep status | None | Active, paused, or invited |
| Social accounts | None | Each rep can have one account per platform |
| Post source | All typed in by the owner | Auto-detected, link submitted, or added by the owner |
| Points per post | Fixed at 10 | 10 by default, and the owner can set points on posts they add |
| Styling | Colors set in Java code | Three CSS files, with colors and fonts as variables |
| Saving | Text file, saved after every change | Sample data in memory only. Changes reset on reload |
| Phones | Not supported | Phone layout below 768px wide |

### Changes made during the build

| Area | Original plan | As built | Why |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Overview metric cards | Included "Points awarded" | Dropped it | It was just approved posts times 10, so it repeated the Approved posts card |
| Overview chart | Weekly bars, 5 weeks | Daily line, last 30 days | Matches the "Last 30 days" subtitle; weekly labels felt clunky |
| Reps table | Included a Platforms column | Removed | Platforms and handles show in the side panel instead |
| Discount code color | Muted, to set it apart from the PR code | Same color as the PR code | Both codes are equally important to the owner |
| Approve all | In the page header | In a review bar above the pending cards | It only applies to Pending, and the header keeps one main button |
| Approve all confirmation | Browser `confirm()` box | The app's own styled popup | The browser box couldn't be styled and said "localhost says" |
| Top bar search | A search box in the top bar | Removed | It searched nothing, and each list page has its own search |
| Top bar color | Light | Deep teal with a white logo and a soft shadow | Gives the page depth and a clear frame |
| Page and sidebar colors | Cream page, sand sidebar | Sand page, cream sidebar | White cards stand out more on sand |
| Posts table dates | One Date column | Posted and Reviewed columns | The owner can see when a post went up and when it was reviewed |
| Shared JavaScript | Not planned | `ui.js` for toasts and the ☰ menu | A second page needed `showToast`, so it moved to one shared file |
| Phone layout | Not planned | Added | Required for the TESD 1100 demo |

