## 4. Page Frame (All Pages)

Every page shares the same frame: a top bar, a sidebar, and the page content.

```text
┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ ☰ Shiver                     (HG) Hippie Goth Stickers │  deep teal top bar
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
│ Overview │  Good evening, Hippie Goth Stickers          │
│ Reps     │  Overview  Last 30 days       [Review posts] │
│ Posts    │  [card] [card] [card] [card]                 │
│ (cream)  │  page content (sand)                         │
```

| Part | Design |
| --- | --- |
| Top bar | Deep teal, 72px tall, white Shiver logo on the left, shop initials circle and shop name on the right, soft shadow underneath |
| Sidebar | Cream, with a mint highlight on the current page and a thin dark sand line on its right edge |
| Page content | Sand background, with white cards that have a soft teal shadow |
| Page header | Page title on the left, the page's one main button on the right |

The frame is split into `<header>` (top bar), `<nav>` (sidebar), and `<main>` (page content). In Phase 5, Shopify supplies its own top bar and menu, so the header can be deleted, the nav becomes Shopify menu links, and `<main>` stays.

## 5. Pages

### Overview (index.html)

```text
Good evening, Hippie Goth Stickers
Overview          Last 30 days                [Review posts]
[Active reps] [Approved posts] [Sales from codes] [Posts to review]
[Approved posts over time chart]  [Needs review list]
[Top reps table: Rep | Posts | Points | Sales]
```

The page reads top to bottom: How am I doing? What's changing? What needs me? Who's driving it?

| Part | Design |
| --- | --- |
| Greeting | "Good morning", "Good afternoon", or "Good evening", plus the shop name, based on the time of day |
| Metric cards | Active reps, Approved posts, Sales from codes ($0 until sales data is added), Posts to review |
| Chart | A line chart of approved posts per day for the last 30 days, with tabs for All and each of the five platforms |
| Needs review | Pending posts, oldest first, each showing the rep and "Posted N days ago". Each row links to the Posts page, and a "Review all posts" link sits at the bottom of the card |
| Top reps | The top 5 reps by total points ever earned, with their approved posts and sales |

### Reps (reps.html)

```text
Reps  6 reps                                    [Add rep]
(All) Active  Paused  Invited
[Search reps.........]  [Sort: Name (A to Z) ▾]
Rep | Discount code | PR code | Points | Sales | Status
```

| Part | Design |
| --- | --- |
| Filter tabs | All, Active, Paused, Invited |
| Search | Filters by rep name, ignoring capital letters |
| Sort | Name (A to Z) by default, or Most points |
| Table | 6 columns. Points is the current balance. Codes use a monospace font. Status shows as a colored badge |
| Empty state | "No reps found" when nothing matches |

**Side panel.** Clicking a rep row opens a panel on the right that floats over the table and dims the rest of the page.

```text
Dante Hicks                                  ✕
notevensupposedtobehere@example.com
(Active)
Discount code   PR code
DANTE30         DANTE10
┌ Social media ────────────────────┐
│ [IG] [YT] [TT] [FB]              │
└──────────────────────────────────┘
┌──────────────────────────────────┐
│ Balance      Posts      Redeemed │
│ 5            3          25       │
└──────────────────────────────────┘
┌ History ─────────────────────────┐
│ Nov 5, 2026   Instagram post +10 │
│ Nov 12, 2026  Redeem...      -25 │
└──────────────────────────────────┘
```

- The email is a link that opens a new email.
- Social media icons link to each account, and the handle shows when hovering.
- Earned history lines are green and link to the post. Redeemed lines are deep teal and show the reason.
- Empty social media and history cards show "No social accounts yet" and "No history yet".

**Add rep popup.** The owner enters a name and email. New reps start as invited, since they haven't joined yet, and get a PR code and a discount code made from their first name in capitals (for example, Brodie Bruce gets `BRODIE10` and `BRODIE30`).

### Posts (posts.html)

```text
Posts                                            [Add post]
(Pending 4)  Approved  Rejected  All

Pending tab:
4 posts waiting for your review  [Approve all]
[post card] [post card] [post card]

Approved, Rejected, and All tabs:
Rep | Platform | Posted | Reviewed | Source | Points | Status (All tab only)
```

The rule for this page is **cards for decisions, tables for records**. Each pending post is its own approve or reject decision, so it gets a card. Reviewed posts are records to look back on, and hundreds of cards would be cluttered, so they go in a table.

```text
┌─────────────────────────────┐
│     [platform icon]         │
│ Jay                         │
│ TikTok · Nov 14, 2026       │
│ Link submitted              │
│ +10 pts   [Approve][Reject] │
└─────────────────────────────┘
```

| Part | Design |
| --- | --- |
| Pending count | A small orange pill on the Pending tab, matching the Posts to review card on Overview |
| Approve and Reject | The card fades out, the count goes down, and a toast confirms the action. A post can only be reviewed once |
| Approve all | Opens a confirmation popup ("Approve 4 posts?") before approving every pending post |
| Source labels | "Auto-detected" (Instagram, Facebook), "Link submitted" (TikTok, YouTube, Substack), "Added by shop owner" |
| Reviewed date | The day a post was approved or rejected, or "—" while pending |
| Status column | Shown on the All tab only, since it would repeat the same word on Approved and Rejected |

**Add post popup.** The owner adds a post by hand, for example when a rep sends a Substack link or the owner spots a post that auto-detect missed. Owner posts are approved right away, since the owner is the reviewer.

| Field | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| Rep | Required. Active and paused reps only, since invited reps haven't joined yet |
| Platform | Required. One of the five platforms |
| Post link | Required. Must start with `https://` |
| Date posted | Required |
| Points | Required. 10 by default, at least 1 |

### Shared pieces

| Piece | Design |
| --- | --- |
| Popups | Built with `<dialog>`, which centers the popup, dims the page, and closes on Esc. The main button is on the right, with Cancel to its left. Forms clear every time a popup closes |
| Toasts | A short message in the bottom right corner for 3 seconds ("Post approved", "Rep added") |
| Empty states | Every list or table that can be empty shows a short message instead of a blank space |

