| Post thumbnails | Shorter, so more cards fit on screen |

## 7. Look and Feel

### Colors

Colors come from the Kelpkin and Shiver colorboard and live as variables in `brand.css`.

| Color | Job |
| --- | --- |
| `#eee6d7` sand | Page background, Paused badge |
| `#f5f1ea` cream | Sidebar, side panel, zebra stripe rows |
| `#ffffff` white | Cards, secondary buttons, top bar text |
| `#c9b994` dark sand | Paused badge border, sidebar edge line |
| `#124049` deep teal | Top bar, headings, primary buttons, badge text, toasts |
| `#557176` muted teal | Muted text such as dates and labels, form field borders |
| `#ccded4` mint | Active nav item, Active badge, active tab, side panel cards |
| `#64a29d` teal | Chart line, Invited badge border, side panel dividers |
| `#336650` earned green | Earned points in history and on post cards |
| `#da7f48` burnt orange | Only for "needs your attention", such as the pending count |

Every text color was checked against its background with the WebAIM contrast formula, aiming for at least 4.5. White text is only used on deep teal.

### Fonts

| Font | Job |
| --- | --- |
| Fredoka | Logo and page titles |
| Inter | Everything else, including chart text |

| Role | Size |
| --- | --- |
| Page title | 24 to 26px |
| Card title | 16px |
| Body | 14px |
| Small | 12px |
| Big number | 28px |

### Design rules

- Spacing comes from an 8px scale: 8, 16, 24, 32, 48.
- 60-30-10 color rule: 60% neutral, 30% structure, 10% accent.
- One main button per page.
- The same pill-style tabs on every page.
- Sentence case for every label, heading, button, and message ("Review posts", not "Review Posts").
- Zebra stripes on data tables.
- One icon set: Bootstrap Icons, chosen because it has all five platform logos, including Substack.
- Realistic sample data, using characters from Kevin Smith films instead of "Test User 1".

## 8. Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Choice | Reason |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Audience | Shop owners first | The owner installs the app and runs the PR program. Reps get the PR Portal later |
| Site type | Inside-the-app dashboard, not a marketing site | Shows what using Shiver is actually like |
| Style | Shopify Polaris look | Shiver will run inside the Shopify admin |
| Post review | Pending posts are approved or rejected | TikTok, YouTube, and Substack links always need a human check |
| Cards or tables | Cards for pending posts, tables for everything else | Cards for decisions, tables for records |
| Rep details | Side panel that floats over the table | Keeps the table in place and avoids a fourth page |
| Chart | Chart.js line chart, daily for 30 days | Axes, tooltips, and resizing come free, and future report charts are one word away |
| Popups | `<dialog>` element | The browser handles centering, dimming, Esc, and keyboard focus |
| Form checks | The browser's built-in validation | No extra code needed for required fields, email, and link format |
| New rep status | Invited | They haven't joined yet, so they can't be credited for posts |
| Points on owner posts | The owner can set them | Gives the owner a way to reward a bigger post |
| Colors | CSS variables in one file | The Shopify version or a dark mode only needs new values |
| Code layout | Data, rules, and display in separate files | The database and Shopify can replace one piece at a time |

### Alternatives considered

| Topic | Option not chosen | Why not |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Audience | Rep-facing PR Portal first | Reps need login, which comes in a later phase |
| Chart | Drawn by hand with HTML and CSS | Much harder for the scatter and pie charts planned for Reports |
| Chart | Bar chart | Line was preferred, and Chart.js can switch with one word |
| Rep details | A separate detail page | More pages and clicks. Kept as a later upgrade |
| Popups | A `<div>` shown and hidden with a class | Centering, dimming, Esc, and focus would all need extra code |
| Confirm box | The browser's `confirm()` | Can't be styled and shows "localhost says" |
| Phone menu | A row of links | A ☰ menu is what phone users expect and saves space |
| Needs review dates | "Posted Nov 12" | A review list cares about how long a post has waited |
| Side panel colors | White, sand, mint, or teal panels | Cream with mint cards matched the sidebar and passed the contrast checks |

