## 10. Build Order

The site was built from the outside in: the frame first, then one page at a time, then polish.

| Step | Build | Reason |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Folders, files, and page skeletons | Every page needs the same structure |
| 2 | `brand.css` | Colors and fonts are used everywhere |
| 3 | `layout.css` | The frame is the same on every page |
| 4 | Sample data and data access functions | Pages need data before they can show anything |
| 5 | Overview page | The first page an owner sees |
| 6 | Reps page and side panel | Builds on the data and rules |
| 7 | Posts page, approve and reject, and Add post | The most interactive page |
| 8 | Overview chart | Needed the posts data and review rules first |
| 9 | Add rep, polish, and the phone layout | Finishing touches once everything worked |

## 11. Testing

Testing was done by hand: a full click-through of every page on desktop and in Chrome's phone view, checks in the browser Console for rules like `approvePost` and `addInvitedRep`, and color contrast checks. Every page passed on both desktop and phone on Nov 19, 2026. See the Testing section of the README for details.

## 12. Known Limitations

- All data is sample data in memory, so every change is lost when the page reloads.
- Sales show $0 until sales data is added.
- Add rep doesn't check for duplicates. Two reps with the same first name get the same codes, and the same email can be added twice.
- Names with apostrophes or accents go into the codes as typed.
- The chart and "Posted N days ago" count back from today, so the sample posts slowly fall off the chart as real days pass.
- The Add post date field allows future dates.
- After adding a post from the Pending tab, the new post doesn't show, since it's approved. The toast is the only sign it was saved.
- Two toasts within 3 seconds share the screen badly, and the first one's timer hides the second early.
- The shop name and initials are typed into each page instead of coming from data.
- The fonts, icons, and Chart.js load from the internet, so the site needs a connection.